# domain
- Viktor is an AI employee reachable at https://api.viktor.com (staging https://staging.viktor.test) through an OpenAI Chat Completions and Responses wire at <host>/api/compat/v1, an Anthropic Messages wire at <host>/api/compat, a hosted stateless Streamable-HTTP MCP server at <host>/mcp, and a native async REST API at <host>/api/public/v1
- a Core is the per-language shared package (TS `packages/core`, Py `python/core`) that owns the Viktor client, canonical message model, streaming parsing, error classification, and fixtures
- an Adapter is a thin per-framework package that depends on one Core and one upstream framework and only converts types and registers with the framework
- a RoutedToolId is a Viktor tool-call id of the form call_vk1_<thread>_<c|t|b>_<suffix> (toolu_vk1_… on the Anthropic wire) that embeds the durable thread id
- a Fixture is a recorded wire exchange (request, response or SSE frames) replayed in unit tests without network
- a LiveContractTest is a test that runs against the real Viktor API when VIKTOR_API_KEY is set and is skipped otherwise

# core/client
- the client reads VIKTOR_API_KEY and VIKTOR_BASE_URL (default https://api.viktor.com) from the environment when not given explicitly @spec
- the client sends the key as `Authorization: Bearer` and always sends model `viktor` @spec
- the client exposes chat completions (sync and streaming), responses (sync and streaming), anthropic messages (sync and streaming), and list models @spec
- the client interface is narrow enough to be re-implemented on top of the Viktor SDK without changing any adapter @spec

# core/continuation
- tool-call ids from Viktor are passed through unchanged in both directions so a follow-up with trailing tool results resumes the durable thread @spec
- the core exposes a helper that extracts the Viktor thread id from a RoutedToolId or a Responses response id, returning null for non-routed ids @spec
- tool declarations are re-sent on every request including resume turns @spec

# core/streaming
- the Chat Completions SSE parser assembles fragmented tool-call arguments by index and yields text deltas, tool calls, finish reason, and optional usage @spec
- an in-stream `{"error":…}` data frame on the Chat Completions wire is surfaced as a typed ViktorRunFailedError carrying the worker message, not as a normal end of stream @spec
- a Responses `response.failed` event and an Anthropic `event: error` are surfaced as ViktorRunFailedError and the trailing `[Stream error: …]` text is dropped @spec
- keep-alive comment lines are ignored by the parser and never surface as content @spec

# core/errors
- HTTP 502 `run_failed` is raised as ViktorRunFailedError with the worker message @spec
- a 200 response with null content and finish_reason stop is surfaced as ViktorEmptyReplyError so callers can distinguish it from an answered turn (opt-in strict mode, default warns) @spec
- 401/403 `{"detail":…}` envelopes are raised as ViktorAuthError with the detail code (invalid_api_key, api_key_inactive, missing scope, identity_denied, compat_api_not_enabled) @spec
- 429 responses are raised as ViktorRateLimitError carrying Retry-After seconds and the code (rate_limit_exceeded, insufficient_quota) @spec
- finish_reason `length` after the 600 s run cap is surfaced as a distinct ViktorRunTimeoutError reason on the result, not silently as a normal stop @spec

# core/images
- user image parts accept https URLs and data URLs; http URLs are rejected client-side with a clear error before the request is sent @spec
- more than 10 image parts in one request is rejected client-side with a clear error @spec

# core/testing
- every Core ships recorded Fixtures for: plain text, streaming text, tool call, tool-result follow-up, image input, run_failed non-streaming, run_failed streaming, rate limit 429, auth 401 @spec
- every Core ships a LiveContractTest that sends a real request when VIKTOR_API_KEY is set and asserts a non-empty reply and a working tool round-trip @spec

# selection
- label: the framework tier list is reproducible from a script with dated inputs
  command: python3 scripts/score_frameworks.py | grep -q "Vercel AI SDK"
  tags: [implemented, m1]
- label: the selection document states a tier, a score and a reason for every candidate framework and protocol surface
  command: for t in "Vercel AI SDK" LangChain "Pydantic AI" Mastra "OpenAI Agents" "Google ADK" LlamaIndex CrewAI AutoGen AG2 "Semantic Kernel" Haystack smolagents DSPy MCP A2A ACP LiteLLM; do grep -q "$t" docs/research/framework-selection.md || exit 1; done
  tags: [implemented, m1]
- label: the design states the featuring path, requirements and artifacts for every Tier 1 framework
  command: grep -q "Featuring plan per Tier 1 framework" docs/design.md
  tags: [implemented, m1]

# delegate-tool
- the delegate tool is named delegate_to_viktor and has the same description and JSON Schema in every adapter and both languages @spec
- the delegate tool creates a Viktor thread over the native REST API, polls the run until it leaves queued/in_progress, and returns status, markdown, json, artifacts, thread_id and run_id @spec
- passing thread_id to the delegate tool sends a follow-up message to that thread instead of creating a new one @spec
- a run that ends in requires_action is returned as a normal tool result whose status is requires_action, not as an error @spec
- the delegate tool stops polling after timeout_seconds and returns status timed_out with the run_id without cancelling the run @spec
- artifacts are returned as display name, content type and a short-lived download URL @spec

# adapters/ai-sdk
- `viktor()` from the AI SDK provider works with generateText and streamText using only VIKTOR_API_KEY @spec
- streamText with tools yields tool-call parts whose toolCallId equals the Viktor routed id byte for byte @spec
- a Viktor in-stream error frame surfaces as an error stream part or thrown error that names run_failed and the worker message @spec
- image file parts with https or data URLs reach Viktor as image_url parts; http URLs are rejected before the request @spec
- the provider object is accepted by Mastra agents and by the OpenAI Agents JS `aisdk()` bridge @draft

# adapters/langchain
- ChatViktor passes the langchain-tests standard unit and integration suites for chat models in Python and JS @draft
- ChatViktor.bind_tools round-trips Viktor tool-call ids unchanged through AIMessage.tool_calls and ToolMessage.tool_call_id @spec
- ChatViktor(use_responses_api=True) threads previous_response_id so multi-turn chat resumes the same Viktor thread @draft
- ViktorDelegateTool is usable as a LangGraph node tool and a handoff helper returns a Command routing to a Viktor agent node @draft

# adapters/pydantic-ai
- ViktorProvider makes OpenAIChatModel and OpenAIResponsesModel talk to Viktor with only VIKTOR_API_KEY set @spec
- ViktorToolset exposes delegate_to_viktor to any pydantic-ai Agent @spec
- Viktor run failures surface as ModelHTTPError or UnexpectedModelBehavior with the worker message preserved @draft

# adapters/mastra
- a Mastra Agent runs with the Viktor model and with viktorDelegateTool registered as a background-capable tool @draft
- a models.dev provider entry for Viktor validates against the models.dev schema @draft

# adapters/openai-agents
- ViktorProvider runs an Agent on the Responses wire by default and on Chat Completions by option, in Python and JS @draft
- viktor_agent() can be used in handoffs and as_tool @draft
- hosted tool types that Viktor cannot execute are rejected with a clear error before the request @draft

# protocols/mcp
- mcp/server.json validates against the official MCP Registry schema and declares the hosted streamable-http remote with a secret Authorization header @draft
- the viktor-mcp stdio bridge forwards JSON-RPC to the hosted endpoint with the key from VIKTOR_API_KEY and contains no tool logic @draft
- a tested MCP recipe exists for every Tier 1 and Tier 2 framework and for Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI, VS Code, Gemini CLI, Windsurf and Zed @draft

# protocols/other
- a generated OpenAI-compatible recipe exists for every Tier 2 and Tier 3 framework and imports or compiles in CI @draft
- a LiteLLM providers.json entry and docs page for Viktor are prepared as a submission kit @draft
- viktor-acp speaks Agent Client Protocol v1 over stdio, maps a session to a Viktor thread, and streams agent_message_chunk updates @draft

# upstream
- every Tier 1 framework has a submission kit with the patch or branch, the exact submission text and a checklist, and nothing is submitted by automation @draft

# maintenance
- CI runs every adapter against the min, latest and next upstream versions and a next failure opens an issue instead of failing the build @draft
- every adapter README states the tested upstream versions and the date, generated from the CI matrix @draft
